1. 00GameDevs effects (https://00gamedevs.com/)
   The 64 effects in fx/ are pixel-art reinterpretations of the 00GameDevs VFX
   library; effect names, descriptions, colours and timings in data/ come from
   its catalogue. The original exported effect code is licensed:

   The MIT License
   Copyright (c) 2026 00GameDevs (@00vchannel)
   (full text identical to the MIT text above)

   The 00GameDevs website UI, branding, avatars and promotional images are not
   covered by that license and are not used here.

2. pixel-plays (https://github.com/amirmushichge/pixel-plays)
   engine/pxfx.js adapts techniques from pixel-plays engine.js: the 4x4 Bayer
   matrix, the hue-shifted ramp rule, the hash/value-noise functions, sphere
   shading, cast shadows and depth-buffer edges.

   MIT License
   Copyright (c) 2026 Amir Mushich
   (full text identical to the MIT text above)

   pixel-plays music is not MIT and is not used here.
